mqtt-monitor (1.1.0-0rc14) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Color RAID cards by state so active arrays read green, rebuilding arrays read amber, and degraded arrays read red.
  * Rework the Home Assistant disk I/O overview into a narrower table with contextual transfer/load labels and calmer rounding.
  * Explain disk load as the share of the latest sample window spent busy serving I/O.

 -- Joao Lino <joao.oliveira.lino@gmail.com> Sun, 12 Apr 2026 20:00:00 +0200

mqtt-monitor (1.1.0-0rc13) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Introduce the V2 runtime with inventory discovery for disks, RAID, mounts, and LXC.
  * Add a first-class issue engine with active and resolved transitions.
  * Publish Home Assistant issue and container entities plus a generated dashboard.
  * Add optional Home Assistant notifications and package the runtime state directory.
  * Compare package versions before self-updating so RC builds do not downgrade to latest stable.
  * Sanitize Home Assistant entity prefixes and skip noisy LXC bind mounts in filesystem discovery.
  * Retry non-NVMe SMART probes across device modes and parse SCSI SMART health correctly.
  * Include mapper-backed monitored mounts in disk discovery and expose logical multipath volumes.
  * Sanitize disk entity IDs so names such as mpatha-part1 produce valid Home Assistant entities.
  * Hide unsupported SMART-only rows from generated dashboard cards for logical volumes.
  * Redesign the generated Home Assistant dashboard into a sections-based operational view.
  * Sanitize filesystem, RAID, container, and issue slugs used in Home Assistant entities.
  * Sync the live Home Assistant monitor view from the generated dashboard source of truth.
  * Declare python3-yaml as a package dependency for dashboard generation.
  * Discover classic-LXC system containers through a narrow privileged helper instead of user-scoped lxc-ls access.
  * Package the helper, install a single-command sudoers rule, and keep the monitor itself unprivileged.
  * Add CAP_SETUID and CAP_SETGID to the service so the helper can elevate through sudo inside the bounded systemd unit.
  * Redesign the generated Home Assistant dashboard around health, storage, services, and disk context.
  * Add disk heat and activity sections so temperatures and busy percentages are easier to interpret at a glance.
  * Shorten Home Assistant entity friendly names to remove repeated monitor prefixes and noisy labels.
  * Restore semantic detail in disk metrics with labels such as SMART Health, Max Temp, and I/O Busy.
  * Add Home Assistant display precision hints so rates and percentages stop showing excessive decimals.
  * Use running-state binary sensors in the dashboard so container tiles can show state-aware coloring.
  * Derive a host-friendly Home Assistant display name when self_name is generic, with an optional explicit override.
  * Replace the percentage-only disk activity overview with disk I/O cards that show read, write, and busy together.
  * Render expected services with explicit green and amber state cards instead of neutral tiles.
  * Add a dense disk I/O table so active disks are easier to scan at a glance.

 -- Joao Lino <joao.oliveira.lino@gmail.com> Sun, 12 Apr 2026 19:35:00 +0200

